\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Your current model 
\f2\fs26 response_voice ~ aspiration_length * place_of_articulation
\f1\fs24  is 
\f0\b valid and appropriate
\f1\b0 . Here's why:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The key issue:
\f1\b0  Aspiration length is not 
\f3\i confounded
\f1\i0  with place of articulation\'97it's 
\f3\i nested
\f1\i0  within it. You have orthogonal manipulation:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 2 levels of aspiration (short/long) \'d7 2 places (bilabial/velar) = 4 conditions\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Each combination exists in your design\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 What you have:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Short bilabial: 25ms\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Long bilabial: 125ms\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Short velar: 50ms\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Long velar: 150ms\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This is a 
\f0\b factorial design
\f1\b0  where aspiration length varies systematically within each place of articulation. The fact that the 
\f3\i absolute
\f1\i0  values differ by place doesn't invalidate the factorial structure\'97you're still contrasting short vs. long within each place.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Why this matters\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Your interaction term (
\f2\fs26 aspiration_length * place_of_articulation
\f1\fs24 ) directly tests your research question: 
\f0\b Does the effect of aspiration length on voicing perception differ between bilabial and velar codas?
\f1\b0  This is likely what you want to know.\
Splitting into separate models would:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Lose statistical power\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Prevent you from formally testing whether the aspiration effect differs by place\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Make it harder to interpret overall patterns\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

